# Disposable job/media content - never tracked, deliberately excluded from this rebuild
client/packages/
client/assets/
client/temp/
client/handout/
client/labor/
client/uploads/
client/advertisements/
dynAPI/tracker/
dynAPI/rendered/
dynAPI/op/rendered/

# Runtime-generated
*.log
*.tmp

# Per-issue XML snapshots (client/xml/{magazineCode}_{issueCode}.xml),
# regenerated on every issue create/delete and pushed to Switch - MariaDB
# is the ground truth, these are disposable outbound artifacts. pmd.xml
# itself IS tracked (it's the whole-dataset export, kept in a known-good
# state deliberately, unlike these per-issue ones).
client/xml/*_*.xml
!client/xml/Publications_Master_Data*.xml

# R3 (PDF rendering) binary + ICC profile bundle - a licensed third-party tool,
# same category as DynaPDF's .so: not application code, not tracked here.
# See SYSTEM_STATE.md's "R3" section for what has to be present at r3API/r3/
# and the permission/capability setup needed for it to actually work.
r3API/r3/
rendertest.pdf
rendertest.jpg
